by javiereguiluz at 2026-07-30T15:26:54Z

Nicolas shared with me the results of an analysis of this code and I fixed all the reported issues:

* The page was unnecesarily large because each log line duplicated their contents (the second copy was added as an HTML attributeand used when you click on "Copy as text"). We now create that log line dynamically with JavaScript when needed.
* Fixed an edge-case in `columnFilters` on `exception.js`: the per-column selection set is now `Object.create(null)`, so logging channels named like some reserved keywords in JavaScript (`constructor`, `toString`, `__proto__`) filter correctly.
* Hide copy buttons when navigator doesn't support the clipboard (`navigator.clipboard` is undefined on non-secure origins, i.e. any http:// dev host that isn't localhost)
* Fixed: `dumpExceptionProperties()` header suppression was order-dependent. It now runs only after a `Data` value was actually dumped
* Fixed `createTabs()` in `exception.js` was too greedy claiming tab groups on the page. It now only claims the ones related to the exception contents

---------------------------------------------------------------------------

by javiereguiluz at 2026-07-30T15:55:05Z

Two more changes:

* Per @stof request, `showExceptionProperties()` in HtmlErrorRenderer now excludes HTTP exceptions via `is_a($class, 'Symfony\Component\HttpKernel\Exception\HttpExceptionInterface', true)` instead of just checking a `Symfony\` prefix
* Added some ignore to `phpstan.dist.neon` instead of making the helpers public. I think it makes more sense if they stay private (because templates aren't really an extension point today)
